---
import InnerLayout from '../../layouts/InnerLayout.astro';
---

<InnerLayout
  title="Custom Engineering | EVO"
  description="EVO custom engineering for purpose-built machinery, modifications, prototypes and multidisciplinary technical systems."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <div class="page-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">CUSTOM ENGINEERING</p>
        <h1>When the standard answer <span>doesn’t fit.</span></h1>
        <p>Some problems need a machine, some need a modification, and some need a completely new technical approach. EVO brings multiple engineering disciplines together to build around the actual requirement.</p>
        <div class="page-hero-actions"><a class="page-button page-button-primary" href="/contact">Discuss a Custom Build ↗</a><a class="page-button page-button-secondary" href="/projects">See Project Examples</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="page-orb"></div><img src="/solutions/solution-custom-engineering.png" alt="" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container page-section-inner">
      <div class="page-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT WE CAN SHAPE</p><h2>Purpose-built for <span>the challenge.</span></h2></div><p>Custom engineering is where mechanical, electrical, automation and software decisions are made as one system instead of separate jobs.</p></div>
      <div class="card-grid-4">
        <article class="content-card"><span>01</span><h3>Custom Machinery</h3><p>Equipment designed around a specific production, handling or process requirement.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span>02</span><h3>Machine Modification</h3><p>Change existing equipment to fit new products, workflows or operating constraints.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span>03</span><h3>Prototype Systems</h3><p>Develop working technical concepts before committing to a larger production build.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span>04</span><h3>Technical Integration</h3><p>Bring sensors, mechanisms, controls and software together into one usable solution.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container page-section-inner">
      <div class="page-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO MACHINE</p><h2>A clear engineering <span>process.</span></h2></div><p>Custom work becomes manageable when decisions are staged and tested instead of trying to solve everything at once.</p></div>
      <div class="process-grid">
        <div class="process-step"><span>01</span><strong>Define</strong><p>Clarify function, limits, safety, throughput and operating conditions.</p></div>
        <div class="process-step"><span>02</span><strong>Concept</strong><p>Shape mechanical, electrical and control architecture.</p></div>
        <div class="process-step"><span>03</span><strong>Build</strong><p>Fabricate, wire, program and integrate the working system.</p></div>
        <div class="process-step"><span>04</span><strong>Validate</strong><p>Test against the real task and refine the weak points.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band"><div class="container cta-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">NOT IN A CATALOGUE?</p><h2>That may be exactly where <span>EVO fits.</span></h2></div><a class="page-button page-button-primary" href="/contact">Start a Conversation ↗</a></div></section>
</InnerLayout>
